From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: a failed recovery masks the interrupt before it powers down

venus_sys_error_handler enables the core's interrupt before it sends HFI's init. When that init fails,
it powers the core down first and only then disables the interrupt. An interrupt in that window makes
venus_isr read the core's registers while core_resets_reset holds it in reset: a synchronous external
abort in interrupt context, a panic. Mask it first, and wait for a handler already running.
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/vcodec/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/vcodec/venus/core.c
@@ -157,10 +157,16 @@
 		failed = true;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Powering down holds the core in reset. An interrupt then would make the handler read its
+	 * registers there: an external abort. The core's interrupt stays masked until the next attempt.
+	 */
+	if (failed)
+		disable_irq(core->irq);
+
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(core->dev);
 
 	if (failed) {
-		disable_irq_nosync(core->irq);
 		dev_warn_ratelimited(core->dev,
 				     "System error has occurred, recovery failed to %s\n",
 				     err_msg);
